From 714ceed9b1b5ca69d8b2d734ccd68b392db210b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:37:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [v2 only] net: cache dictionary-versioned independent
 compressed block frames

Add FIN/BINARY RSV2 independent zstd frames beside raw and connection-history RSV1 messages. Carry format and immutable native dictionary version, enforce configured plain/wire bounds and explicit decoder-window limits, and reject malformed or mixed reserved flags. Cache block encodings under exact payload and dictionary identity with bounded shared LRU ownership.

Fold the window, standard-frame, configured-cap and streaming-control refinements into this owner. Preserve N5 native dictionary2 and retained legacy dictionary1. Unit and Python decoders cover both forms; unchanged negative controls reproduce the removed-guard failures.

Original-Source: d261bfa4ae with ce34616bfc,9ab2f30970,3ab4a97ce6,2660622bae,5f1407a140 folded. Integration: omit temporary dictionary API/version1 scaffolding; retain corrected-base N1 cap owner and its streaming regression explicitly under threshold0.
